      <memberdef kind="function" id="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_zero_copy_frame_builder_1a32a01d3e6dd022e93686a04bfd28971d" prot="public" static="no" const="yes" explicit="no" inline="no" virt="non-virtual">
        <type>ssize_t</type>
        <definition>ssize_t themis::network::ZeroCopyFrameBuilder::writeToWithSendfile</definition>
        <argsstring>(int socket_fd, int payload_fd, off_t payload_offset=0, size_t sendfile_threshold=65536) const</argsstring>
        <name>writeToWithSendfile</name>
        <qualifiedname>themis::network::ZeroCopyFrameBuilder::writeToWithSendfile</qualifiedname>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>socket_fd</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>int</type>
          <declname>payload_fd</declname>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>off_t</type>
          <declname>payload_offset</declname>
          <defval>0</defval>
        </param>
        <param>
          <type>size_t</type>
          <declname>sendfile_threshold</declname>
          <defval>65536</defval>
        </param>
        <briefdescription>
<para>Large-payload path: write header via write(2), then payload via sendfile(2) / splice(2) (Linux) or sendfile(2) (macOS/FreeBSD). </para>
        </briefdescription>
        <detaileddescription>
<para>For payloads ≥ <computeroutput>sendfile_threshold</computeroutput> bytes and where <computeroutput>payload_fd</computeroutput> is a valid open file descriptor, this method:<orderedlist>
<listitem><para>Writes the 12-byte header with write(2).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>Transfers <computeroutput>payload_size_</computeroutput> bytes from <computeroutput>payload_fd</computeroutput> starting at <computeroutput>payload_offset</computeroutput> using sendfile(2) (Linux / BSD) or splice(2) (Linux pipe path) — zero userspace copy.</para>
</listitem></orderedlist>
</para>
<para>Falls back to <computeroutput><ref refid="classthemis_1_1network_1_1_zero_copy_frame_builder_1a1b238f84d67640fab3aca73d3477a64d" kindref="member">writeTo()</ref></computeroutput> if:<itemizedlist>
<listitem><para><computeroutput>payload_fd</computeroutput> &lt; 0 (caller signals: not file-backed).</para>
</listitem><listitem><para><computeroutput>payload_size_</computeroutput> &lt; <computeroutput>sendfile_threshold</computeroutput>.</para>
</listitem><listitem><para>sendfile(2) / splice(2) fails with EINVAL / ENOSYS (e.g., the fd is a socket, not a regular file — kernel constraint).</para>
</listitem></itemizedlist>
</para>
<para>R15: Removed noexcept guarantee to allow exception-safe buffer allocation in sendfile fallback path. Callers must handle std::bad_alloc if buffer allocation fails during fallback to pread + write.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="param"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>socket_fd</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Destination socket file descriptor. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>payload_fd</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Source file descriptor for sendfile. Pass -1 to force fallback to writev. </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>payload_offset</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Starting offset in the source file (bytes). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
<parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>sendfile_threshold</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Minimum payload size to use sendfile (bytes). Default: 65536 (64 KiB). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
<simplesect kind="return"><para>Total bytes written (header + payload) on success, or -1 on error (errno set by the failing syscall). </para>
</simplesect>
<parameterlist kind="exception"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>std::bad_alloc</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>if memory allocation fails in fallback path </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
